{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["<b>He who disciplines</b> — who disciplined the men of the Flood, and the generation of the Dispersion, and the men of Sodom." "<b>Will He not reprove</b> — you. And the meaning: if you are many, He has already disciplined many like you, for He knows all your deeds, for He is the one who teaches man knowledge, and behold, the knowledge of man compared to the knowledge of the Most High is as nothing. And how can man think that HaShem does not see and does not understand, when He is the one who teaches man knowledge?! And it is known that knowledge is from Him, therefore after this: \"YHWH knows the thoughts of man, that they are vanity\" (Psalms 94:11), as He said: \"He who planted the ear\" (Psalms 94:9)."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 94, :notes {1 "Resolved ה' as YHWH in the embedded Psalm citation; the final quotation 'He who planted the ear' cites Psalm 94:9, which appears in the same psalm, preceding verse 11."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:37:14.502561722Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}